@page "/optimistic-actions"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Optimistic Actions</PageTitle>

<h1>Optimistic Actions</h1>

<p>Trace of the <em>optimistic-actions</em> example (o caso de rollback que o corpus original
    does not). In BRHC, the button shows the <em>pending</em> state via <code>data-indicator</code>/
    <code>data-attr:disabled</code> enquanto o POST voa; o servidor confirma o valor ou reverte-o
    por <code>patch-elements</code> no <code>#items-table</code> - o "Item 3" falha sempre, e o
    the rollback stays visible. Here C# does the same: the pending badge is component state and
    SignalR delivers the diff. <strong>Teaching note:</strong> in Blazor the optimistic state is a
    variable (no declared signal); rollback is assigning the previous value - the equivalent of
    the Datastar rollback patch.
</p>

<div class="demo-box">
    @if (serverError is not null)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-danger py-2">@serverError</div>
    }

    <table class="table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Item</th>
                <th>Value</th>
                <th>Action</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var item in items)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td>@item.Label</td>
                    <td>@item.Value</td>
                    <td>
                        <button class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" disabled="@item.Pending" @onclick="() => Apply(item)">
                            @(item.Pending ? "pending…" : "+10")
                        </button>
                    </td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

@code {
    private sealed record OptimisticItem(int Id, string Label, int Value, bool Pending = false, bool Failed = false);

    // "Item 3" falha sempre - alimenta o caminho de rollback (igual ao Kotlin).
    private readonly List<OptimisticItem> items = new()
    {
        new(0, "Item 1", 10),
        new(1, "Item 2", 20),
        new(2, "Item 3", 30, Failed: true),
        new(3, "Item 4", 40),
    };

    private string? serverError;

    // Equivalent to BRHC's POST /optimistic-actions/action: pending -> confirmation
    // or rollback; the error badge arrives as the patch of the `error` signal.
    private async Task Apply(OptimisticItem item)
    {
        serverError = null;
        var index = items.FindIndex(x => x.Id == item.Id);
        var willFail = items[index].Failed;

        items[index] = items[index] with { Pending = true };
        StateHasChanged();

        await Task.Delay(600); // simulated latency, as in the Kotlin example

        items[index] = willFail
            ? items[index] with { Pending = false }
            : items[index] with { Value = items[index].Value + 10, Pending = false };

        if (willFail)
        {
            serverError = "Servidor recusou: falha simulada (rollback)";
        }
        StateHasChanged();
    }
}